From: Gilly1970 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: extend manual RX calibration to E2 silicon

AN7581 E2 silicon (PRODUCT_ID 2) can still require the manual USXGMII
RX calibration path used by earlier revisions. On affected Gemtek
boards the hardware/default path can leave stale TFCK/DA_RX state and
produce intermittent receive-side stalls on the direct 10G GDM port.

The same calibration routine has been exercised on an affected E2
Gemtek W1700K with 16/16 automatic LAN2 RX tests completing at about
204--211 MB/s with no failures. Keep hardware calibration for E3 and
later silicon, but include E2 in the manual path.

This is especially relevant to Gemtek AN7581 boards whose direct 10G
LAN port uses the same Airoha PCS/USXGMII block as XR1710G LAN2.

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -2068,5 +2068,5 @@
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		if (FIELD_GET(AIROHA_SCU_PRODUCT_ID, val) < 0x2)
+		if (FIELD_GET(AIROHA_SCU_PRODUCT_ID, val) < 0x3)
 			priv->manual_rx_calib = true;
